V$, say $v_i = f(y_i)$, then $f(y_2 + v_1) = f(y_2)+v_1 = v_2+v_1$, so $v_1+v_2 \in V$. Setting $x=-v$ in $f(x+v)=f(x)+v$ gives $f(-v)=c-v \in V$, hence $-v \inV$.

